// ?getAircraftPath@Pathfinder@@QAEPAVPath@@PBVObject@@PBUCoord3D@@@Z
// partial score=0.204 date=2026-09-28
// cl: /DNDEBUG /MD /EHsc
//
// Retail 0x003E17A0: Pathfinder::getAircraftPath (caller 0x002712D0 aircraft
// branch).  Rewritten 2026-09-28 as real C++ on the layout and helper set of
// the landed sibling checkPathCost (PathfinderStepD4F90.cpp): same
// PathfindCell/PathfindCellInfo view, inline allocateInfo, the pinned
// rva003D6400/rva003D6490/rva003DB900/rva003F6C30/rva003F6F10 helpers, no
// member-pointer unions.  Control flow read from the retail disassembly.
// Measured: 1449 B vs 1514, 1140 non-reloc diffs, shape 0.843 (stash was
// 1501 B / 1199 / 0.737).
//
// Remaining blocker is the frame: retail 0x5c with heavy slot sharing
// (start/adjacent at +0x44, destination/neighborFlags at +0x38,
// cell/newCellCoord at +0x30, startCellNdx.x/cellCount at +0x14, the dead
// `to` argument slot holding the open-list cell and the new-Path $T).  Ours is
// 0x80 with no aggregate sharing.  Measured with /FAsc: VC7.1 does pack these
// sibling-block aggregates for this exact body when the inner loop is cut
// down (dropping the m_costSoFar store packs start/adjacent and
// startCellNdx/neighborFlags), and packing also depends on the EH mode
// (/EHa packs sibling blocks in functions with a new-expression where /EHsc
// does not, e.g. { int a[2]; f(a); } { int b[2]; f(b); } return new P;).
// So the packing is reachable; what retail's source did to stay under the
// limit is not found.

typedef int Int;
typedef unsigned int UnsignedInt;
typedef unsigned short UnsignedShort;
typedef bool Bool;
typedef float Real;

#define PATHFIND_CELL_SIZE_F 10.0f

